{"question": "How do I configure and lock the annual fiscal year budget?", "topic": "annual_budget", "seconds": 16.437, "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [{\"id\": \"guide:annual_budget:0\", \"title\": \"Configure annual Office Budget and fiscal year\", \"text\": \"Open Office Budget for the correct office and fiscal year. Build annual sections/accounts, review totals and cash limits, save the draft, then use the authorized lock action before funding work.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:annual_budget:2\", \"title\": \"Configure annual Office Budget and fiscal year\", \"text\": \"Locked or closed years have stricter editing rules. Use the permitted adjustment action and reason where available, rather than replacing a budget to hide a commitment or bypass a year guard.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:budget:0\", \"title\": \"Does setting a task Budget consume Office Budget?\", \"text\": \"Click Budget or Set budget for the task in Main table. The appointed Head of the responsible office", "passed": false}
{"question": "How do I liquidate an advance?", "topic": "settlement", "seconds": 16.0, "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [{\"id\": \"guide:settlement:1\", \"title\": \"Liquidation, receipts and unused cash\", \"text\": \"The authorized reviewer checks the current package. Accounting settlement/posting is separate from merely uploading receipts; an outstanding advance is not verified actual spending.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:budget_position:1\", \"title\": \"Available budget, commitments and cash returns\", \"text\": \"For example, 10,000 pesos of available annual authority with 3,000 committed leaves 7,000 for new commitments. Settling a 500-peso advance as 400 spent and 100 returned does not release the unused commitment.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:settlement:0\", \"title\": \"Liquidation, receipts and unused cash\", \"text\": \"After using released cash, submit liquidation or settlement with actual expenses, required receipt", "passed": false}
{"question": "How do I correct a rejected cash request?", "topic": "cash_rejection", "seconds": 15.906, "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [{\"id\": \"guide:cash_rejection:0\", \"title\": \"Reject, correct and re-request petty cash\", \"text\": \"If cash is rejected or returned, open the recorded feedback, correct the purpose, amount or supporting information, then use the available revision or resubmission action.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:cash_rejection:1\", \"title\": \"Reject, correct and re-request petty cash\", \"text\": \"Rejection does not authorize release. Check the saved request state and pool before requesting again; a duplicate request is not the same as correcting a rejected one.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:cash_rejection:2\", \"title\": \"Reject, correct and re-request petty cash\", \"text\": \"Cancel or delete only in permitted states. Released advances, settlements and audit records follow the financial workflow rather than being erased", "passed": false}
{"question": "When can Accounting release a scheduled tranche?", "topic": "cash_release", "seconds": 15.562, "raw": "{\"source_ids\": [{\"id\": \"guide:cash_release:1\", \"title\": \"Voucher and cash release schedules\", \"text\": \"Releases are checked against current authority, calendar, daily and request limits. A future scheduled tranche is not already cash in the recipient's hands.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:cash_release:2\", \"title\": \"Voucher and cash release schedules\", \"text\": \"An available schedule override requires the permitted actor, selected tranche and audited reason. It changes release timing, not unrelated approval or posting authority.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide:access:1\", \"title\": \"Voucher & Cash Releases\", \"text\": \"Authorized Accounting staff use Voucher & Cash Releases to inspect approved requests, voucher details and scheduled tranches. Verify recipient, remaining amount and permitted release date before confirming.\"}, {\"id\": \"guide", "passed": false}
